        "original_id": "15ce1eb1-f5ef-5207-ab4c-197547016de9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jude Law, Jack Black, Eli Wallach, Shannyn Sossamon, Edward Burns, Rufus Sewell, Kenneth Branagh\n- Films: The Holiday, Hamlet, The Woodlanders, Dangerous Beauty, Dark City, A Knight's Tale, The Illusionist, Tristan and Isolde, Martha, Meet Frank, Daniel and Laurence, Garden State\n- Music: Details (album), \"Let Go\"\n- Roles: Graham, Miles, Fortinbras\n\nFacts:\n- Rufus Sewell was born on 29 October 1967 and is an English actor.\n- In 1996, Rufus Sewell appeared as Fortinbras in Kenneth Branagh's film rendition of Hamlet.\n- Rufus Sewell has also appeared in the films The Woodlanders, Dangerous Beauty, Dark City, A Knight's Tale, The Illusionist, Tristan and Isolde, and Martha, Meet Frank, Daniel and Laurence.\n- In The Holiday, Jude Law and Jack Black were cast as the leading men Graham and Miles.\n- In The Holiday, Eli Wallach, Shannyn Sossamon, Edward Burns, and Rufus Sewell played key supporting roles.\n- The song \"Let Go\" from the album Details featured in the soundtrack for Garden State and in the film The Holiday.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
